attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on the cellulose synthase genes.** Column 0, `bcsF`, is a spine column carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 99% of calls {S1}. The model names 99.6% of them, at 0.17 bits {S1}.

@variable **The first fork is at `bcsE`**, column 1, carried by 85%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. Then columns 3 to 4, `bcsQ` to `bcsA`, are variable, carried by 83 to 87%, [[cellulose biosynthesis]] {S4, Q}. Through columns 49 to 51 a branch of 3 families runs in 11 to 14%, and through columns 64 to 73 a branch of 10 families runs in 10 to 12%, [[copper]] {S12.b49, S14.b64, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 93 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.21 against 0.33 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 1, `bcsE`, a fork column, 0.87 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 53 to 79, `yhiI` to `livJ`, are carried by 36 to 90%, fewest named at column 79, 85% {S14}. The last column is `livJ`, in 36% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.27 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.51 against 0.19 bits, and names fewer genes, 89% against 93% {C}.

